  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "These are mainly accessibility requests.\n\n[Time to Destroy]\n\nThe time limit for what you write before it starts to disappear seems to be 30 seconds at the moment. \n\nThis is often too short when you want to write a lot. \n\nEspecially for 2-byte characters, it may take more time to write just one character. \n\nI would suggest that a few minutes would be more realistic for these characters before they start disappearing.\n\n[Erase]\n\nCurrently, the only option to erase is to turn off Frosted Scribe, which deletes everything. \n\nThis is often not ideal when you are writing complicated 2-byte characters and want to delete just a part of your last entry to correct a mistake. \n\nPerhaps adding a function to erase the last line with a specific action on the Frosted symbol would be beneficial.\n\n[Color]\n\nIf there are several people using the pen at the same time, it's easy for things to get mixed up. \n\nI'm not suggesting we have an unlimited choice of colors, but it would be a good idea to provide a few color options for better visibility and usability.",
